From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:42:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,tristar-charger: Add the
 D2089

The iPad mini 2 (J85) charges through the same Tristar port controller,
with a D2089 PMIC. iOS 12.5.8 AppleD2089PMU drives the D2089's charger
as AppleD2207PMU drives the D2207's: connection and charger state at
0x60 and 0x62, the input-current limit at 0x4c0, the ADC at 0x500, and
ADC completion on PMU event 89. The node therefore has the same banks
and interrupts as on the iPad Air 2.

Add apple,d2089-tristar-charger, with apple,j85-tristar-charger for the
board.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml  | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
index 8e4acf9f7..4d9155868 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
@@ -11,10 +11,10 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |
   Charging on Apple devices whose Lightning port uses a Tristar (NXP CBTL1610)
-  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC, such as the iPad 5 and iPad 6 (D2365)
-  and the iPad Air 2 (D2207). The PMICs have the same charger functions at
-  different register addresses, so the compatible names the PMIC. The
-  node is a child of the PMIC. It identifies the attached source through the
+  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC, such as the iPad 5 and iPad 6 (D2365),
+  the iPad Air 2 (D2207) and the iPad mini 2 (D2089, laid out as the D2207).
+  The PMICs have the same charger functions at different register addresses,
+  so the compatible names the PMIC. The node is a child of the PMIC. It identifies the attached source through the
   Tristar and the PMIC ADC and sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot
   leaves at 100 mA. PMU events come from the PMIC's event interrupt
   controller (the PMIC GPIO node).
@@ -38,6 +38,9 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - const: apple,j81-tristar-charger
           - const: apple,d2207-tristar-charger
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,j85-tristar-charger
+          - const: apple,d2089-tristar-charger
 
   reg:
     items:
